PROPOSAL: trusted CLI verification preparation reads candidate tracked files from restored/verified artifact, verifies blob hashes and modes, rejects symlinks/gitlinks/unsafe paths and bounds total 32MiB/10000 entries. Agents image builder accepts this host snapshot. It builds an in-memory deterministic tar with only generated Dockerfile and candidate files. Fixed Dockerfile FROM pinned local base sha256, COPY candidate/ into unique cryptographically random reserved directory, WORKDIR that directory; no RUN/no candidate Dockerfile execution/no network. Base image Config.OnBuild and Volumes must be empty, pinned ID confirmed, daemon pinned. Build API legacy version1 networkmode none pull false; parse aux ID and inspect resulting image exact label/input digest, OnBuild/Volumes, base config. Image receipt binds tree/content digest, archive digest, base ID, image ID, candidate dir, daemon. Host-owned private evidence. Tests opt-in contained config only, defaults unchanged. Graph broker adds contained registration kind executing through existing G04 wrapper. It allocates invocation ID, beforeEffect marks actual ledger running, passes host scope/run/generation/effectKey/invocation to executor factory; bindingRef hashes candidate binding+image+acceptance+actual identity. Container Config.WorkingDir is explicit receipt path, fixed command acceptance; spec digest binds it. Return separate contained result (no forged POSIX command receipt) including actual exitCode/cancelled/stopReceipt digest/image binding. Persist and load compare expected effect/candidate/acceptance, invocation, generation; no model report can provide this. Business failure classification explicit. Start/stop/read use host authority with fence/cancel grants. No worker-stop or G15 takeover in this slice; no replay on unknown. Add focused negative tests and real Linux Graph broker candidate pass/fail/abort test, full Loop and Kimi source audit.

